      "detail": "type List<T>",
      "documentation": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "value": "Functions for the built-in `List<T>`, a persistent RRB-tree vector\n(§3.8, D-039, ADR-0018).\n\n`List` is a builtin item whose home module is this one (D-447). The\nkernels, the functions that build, read or cut the tree, are runtime\nfunctions with required costs (D-274, D-300). Every other function is\nwritten in Cheby over the kernels and over list patterns, whose `..rest`\nshares structure with the list (D-053). Each of them is tail-recursive,\nso none grows the stack with the length of a list (D-094), and none of\nthe kernels calls back into Cheby."
      },
